Package: resman
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: Francesco Defilippo <francesco@defilippo.org>
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Homepage: https://github.com/fdefilippo/resman
Description: per-user CPU, memory and IO observer and manager for cgroups v2
 ResMan monitors Linux resource usage and applies cgroups v2 limits on
 supported ownership models. The systemd-native adapter preserves session
 ownership and applies flat CPU Points with CPU_ROOT_POINTS=100. RAM and I/O
 require complete resource authority. ResMan never migrates PIDs; hosts without
 authoritative systemd enforcement remain observation-only.
 .
 It provides Prometheus metrics, PSI event-driven control, configuration
 hot reload, SQLite history, limit notifications and an optional MCP server.
 .
 Read /usr/share/doc/resman/UPGRADING.md before upgrading from 1.25.x through 1.34.1 to 1.35.4.
